Problem
My Google Photos slideshow picker works and successfully selects photos, showing "SLIDESHOW - 7 Pictures", but the screen remains completely black. The images are not rendering.
Root Cause
The GooglePhotosWidget component is trying to use photo.mediaFileUri or photo.previewUri directly as the src attribute in <img> tags. These URIs require OAuth authentication and cannot be loaded directly in image elements without proper authorization headers.
Required Fix
Modify the GooglePhotosWidget component to:

Fetch authenticated images: When photos are selected, fetch each image using the access token with proper authorization headers
Convert to blob URLs: Convert the authenticated image data to blob URLs that can be used in <img> tags
Cache the blob URLs: Store these blob URLs instead of (or alongside) the original URIs so they persist across renders
Clean up blob URLs: Properly revoke blob URLs when clearing the slideshow or when component unmounts

Implementation Requirements
The fix should be in the GooglePhotosWidget component around line 636 in the fetchSessionItems function and the rendering section around line 710-728.
Key changes needed:

After fetching session items, download each image with authentication:

javascriptconst fetchImageAsBlob = async (uri: string) => {
  const response = await fetch(uri, {
    headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + accessToken }
  });
  const blob = await response.blob();
  return URL.createObjectURL(blob);
};

Process all images to create blob URLs:

javascriptconst itemsWithBlobs = await Promise.all(
  validItems.map(async (item) => {
    const uri = item.mediaFileUri || item.previewUri;
    const blobUrl = await fetchImageAsBlob(uri);
    return { ...item, blobUrl };
  })
);

Update the photo rendering to use blobUrl:

javascript<img 
  src={photo.blobUrl} 
  alt={photo.filename || ""} 
  className="w-full h-full object-cover" 
/>

Add cleanup when clearing slideshow:

javascriptconst clearSlideshow = () => {
  // Revoke all blob URLs to free memory
  photos.forEach(photo => {
    if (photo.blobUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(photo.blobUrl);
  });
  setPhotos([]);
  localStorage.removeItem(PHOTOS_CACHE_KEY);
  setCurrentIndex(0);
};
Important Notes

Make sure to add loading state while fetching and converting images to blobs
Add error handling for failed image downloads
Log progress in the photos debug log for troubleshooting
Consider showing a loading indicator for each image being processed
The blob URLs should be stored in localStorage along with the photo metadata, but note that blob URLs don't persist across page reloads - you may need to regenerate them on component mount if loading from cache

Expected Result
After this fix, the slideshow should display the selected photos correctly instead of showing a black screen.

